.SH NAME
.PP
auto-select-sound-device - Select a default sound device

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-select-sound-device
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
None
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-select-sound-device
command lists available sounds devices and prompts the user to
select a default.  The current default is indicated in the listing.
Pressing return without indicating a device results in no change.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

